A||N||4||wwh0001||DASH LIGHTS||||5||
Z||000000||wwh0001||12-20-1999||10:45 AM||||More problems with my 87GT. I fixed the oil leaks ( valve covers) thanks to help from this board. So I am asking for help again. <BR>My Dash lights will not come on when I turn the headlights on. All exterior lights come on as does the light for the shift console ( auto) ashtray and cig light. The Clock light goes out when the headlights are turned on and comes back on when they are turned off. The dimmer switch will turn on the overhead courtesy lights.<BR>I checked the fuses and they are ok. If the headlamp switch or dimmer switch were bad it seems as though the other lights would also not work. The headlamp switch is turning on the cig and shifter lights and the dimmer switch will turn on the courtesy lights.<BR>No recent wiring work and no optional equipment hooked up. Problem just happened. Can't believe all dash lights would burn out at same time.<BR>Any thoughts about where to look? Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bill Osmer||12-20-1999||10:49 AM||||Have you checked the "Dimmer electronics"? There is a circuit that the dimmer rheostat connects to that has a larger transistor w/heatsink that actually does the dimming. If that circuit goes bad/open, the IP lights go out. It's located under the passenger's side IP, I think||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||12-20-1999||01:06 PM||||Well I too had that problem and located the transistor in question under the dash on the drivers side. It's is wedged up there between the steering column and the center console. It's silver in appearance and attached by two screws. I just pulled mine and cleaned everything up and put it back together after calling the dealer and finding out it's a $40 part that has to be special ordered. That was about 4 months ago and they have worked fine ever since.  Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000003||wwh0001||12-20-1999||02:42 PM||||Thanks for the comments. I'll check it out tonight||||reg||7
Z||000004||wwh0001||12-21-1999||08:52 AM||||This board scores again. I took off the transistor that was in the heat sink. Cleaned off the posts and my dash lights work again. If only everything could be this easy. Thanks.||||reg||6
